1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Hoversten&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GSsr=81&GRid=53153691&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Hoversten was born in 1824 and was the youngest of eight children born to Johannes and Anna Hoversten. He became a tanner and worked at some time in Olen, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1849 he married Martha Halvorsdatter-Bromeland. They had seven children, in the following order: 
2 CONT *Johannes K (who went by the last name of Johnson), 
2 CONT *Martha (died in infancy), 
2 CONT *Andreas, 
2 CONT *Martha,
2 CONT *Anna,
2 CONT *Ingeborg, and 
2 CONT *Bertha.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut's wife Martha died in 1864, leaving 6 small children. In 1866 Knut married Eli Tobiasdatter, the family's maid. Knut and Eli had three children in Norway: 
2 CONT *Torbjorn (died in infancy), 
2 CONT *Karina, and 
2 CONT *Ellen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut, Eli and eight children immigrated from Norway to the U.S.A. in 1871. They sailed to Montreal, Canada, and then took a train from Montreal to LaSalle County, Illinois. Sometime after that they moved to Lee County, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut farmed near Stewart, Illinois, until his death in 1884. He is buried in the Evangelical Lutheran Cemetery, located five miles east of Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Knut Hoversten:
2 CONT *Immigration: 1871, Came from Norway to U.S.A. via Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Knut Hoversten and Eli Tobiasdatter:
2 CONT *Marriage: 1866, Norway.
