1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Hoversten&GSiman=1&GScid=2149121&GRid=97960376&
2 CONT
2 CONT Emmanuel Hoversten was the son of Knut Hoversten and Eli Tobiasdatter Hoversten.He was born in 1884 in Illinois, and moved with his mother to Hamilton County, Iowa, after his father's death in Illinois. In Iowa, he married his fir
2 CONC st cousin, Elizabeth Serby Anderson, in 1902.The two of them had 11 children, in the following order: Elmer Truman, Ruby, Joseph, Esther Leone, Bernard, Ernest, Gladys, Myrtle, a daughter still living in 2010, Ruth, and Evelyn. Th
2 CONC e family were devout members of the Lutheran Church.Emmanuel was a farmer, and beginning in 1918 he, his wife and children lived on a farm located near Radcliffe, Iowa.After his wife Elizabeth died in 1925, Emmanuel continued to l
2 CONC ive on the farm with his children, and he never remarried.He was buying the farm from his brother Thomas Hoversten when the Great Depression hit, and in 1936 he found himself unable to make further payments.  Having lost the farm,
2 CONC  Emmanuel moved to Gifford, Iowa, that year.He bought a filling station in Gifford; later he purchased a hardware and general store.He ran the two enterprises and lived behind the store.After some years, he phased out general merc
2 CONC handise and focused on hardware sales.  In the early 1950s, Emmanuel became ill with heart disease, and he died in Gifford in 1952.He was buried alongside his wife, Elizabeth, in Rose Grove Cemetery, near Williams, Iowa. More Abou
2 CONC t Emmanuel Hoversten and Elizabeth Serby Anderson: Marriage: 1902, Hamilton County, Iowa.
