1 NOTE
2 CONT January 23, 1902 - A large deal was consumated here yesterday by which Mr. Elias Faa of Newburg becomes the proprietor of the implement business formerly owned by T. T. Bergh.  Mr. Bergh has been in the machine business in this pl
2 CONC ace for about twenty-three years and has made a decided success; he will still retain the Music business and will give this his undivided attention.  We welcome Mr. Faa to our city and wish him success in his venture.
2 CONT
2 CONT September 12, 1907 - E. T. Faa has sold his harness shop here to Wilbur Nelson of Caledonia, who will conduct the business hereafter . Mr. Nelson is well-known here and needs no introduction at our hands having been employed here 
2 CONC a few years ago.  We wish the new management success.
2 CONT
2 CONT March 5, 1908 - E. T. Faa of Newburg who was formerly engaged in business at this place, called on friends in the city Saturday and while in town made the Herald office a pleasant and profitable call.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 109 - O. S. Johnson - Tore's Faa's son, Elias T. Faa lived in Spring Grove some years ago.  Elias was in partnership with Gustav Glasrud handling farm machinery.  They also had a saddle making shop together. Elias sold out hi
2 CONC s share to Gustav and moved away.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 30 NOV 2014
3 TIME 07:04:44
