1 NAME Cecelia Johannesdatter /Byrkja/
2 GIVN Cecelia Johannesdatter
2 SURN Byrkja
2 _MARNM Christian
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Roland Cem.
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 FEB 1843
2 PLAC Byrkja
2 ADDR
3 CITY Årdal
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 OCT 1930
2 ADDR
3 CITY Roland
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU immigrated 1844.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Årdal II page 52 Byrkja (44b).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/115184985/cecelia-christian
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration Year: 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John and Elizabeth "Betsy" A. Pierson (both of Norway)
2 CONT
2 CONT See husband John Christian's record for list of known children
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary source: The Roland Record, Roland, Story County, Iowa October 30, 1930 "MRS. CECELIA CHRISTIAN With the death of Mrs. Cecelia Christian Saturday, one of the oldest residents of the community passed away. She came to Ameri
2 CONC ca 86 years ago and after several years in Illinois, came to this community, where she has since resided. She was over 87 years of age at the time of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecelia Pierson was born at Ordal, near Stavanger, Norway, February 17, 1843. The following year she came to America with her parents and lived near Lisbon, Ill. After a few years the family moved to Story County, Iowa, where she 
2 CONC continued to live until her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was confirmed by Rev. Rasmussen at the present site of Story City, before a church had been built in the community. In 1860 she was united in marriage to John Christian. To this union nine children were born of whom seven prec
2 CONC eded her in death, two died in infance, two in early childhood, Bertha Serena in June 1899, Alice Elizabeth in March 1901, Jonas in Novebmer 1929.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband passed away in February 1908. She continued to reside at the old home of her son Edward R. Christian until seventeen years ago. Since then she has made her home with her son Jonas and family. She was taken sick Monday 
2 CONC evening, October 20th and died Saturday morning, October 25th at the age of 87 years 8 months and 8 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT She leaves to mourn her passing, two sons, Otis H., of Stratford, S.D., and Edward B. of roland. Also sixteen grandchildren and twelve great grandchildren, and one brother at Windom, Minn., besides many relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was held Tuesday at the Christian home northwest of town and at Salem church, Rev. Olaf Holen officiating. Interment was made in the Roland cemetery."
