1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Webster City Freeman Journal, May 8 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie Hoversten, 100, of Webster City, died Sunday, May 7, 2006 at the Hamilton Hospital. Funeral services will be held at 1:30 p.m. Thursday at Trinity Lutheran Church, with Rev. Doug Tiffany officiating. Burial will be in the R
2 CONC ose Grove Cemetery, southwest of Williams.Visitation will be one hour before the service. Foster Funeral and Cremation Center in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie Evelyn Hoversten, daughter of Chris and Sina Knutson Hoversten, was born February 25, 1906 near Williams. She graduated from Williams High School, received a degree in education from Iowa State Teachers College and her mast
2 CONC ers from Drake University. She had taught in a rural school near Williams, in the Williams Public School, Lacona Public school, Ottumwa schools and for 24 years taught in Des Moines schools.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by several nieces and nephews. She was preceded in death by sisters, Ella Fjetland; Nora Erickson; Sena Andersen; brothers, Kane, Clarence and Alvaun Hoversten.
