1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.brainerddispatch.com/obituaries/3885108-chester-hoversten 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial record and obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=hoverste&GSpartial=1&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=155115328&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Mar. 7, 1922 Lynd Lyon County Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Nov. 16, 2015 Northfield Rice County Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Chester Hoversten
2 CONT
2 CONT B. Tuesday, March 7, 1922 D. Monday, November 16, 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Chester E. Hoversten was born on March 7, 1922, on the family farm near Lynd, Minnesota, to Elias and Martha (Johannesen) Hoversten. He graduated from high school in Minneota, MN. Worked at the Marshall Cafe for one year to e
2 CONC arn money for college.
2 CONT
2 CONT He obtained his bachelors degree in chemistry from Augsburg College in 1944 and Masters in divinity from Augsburg Seminary in 1947. He married Phyllis Johnson from Hendricks, MN in 1945. He attended graduate school in psychology a
2 CONC t the University of Minnesota and accepted his first call to start a mission congregation in Russellville (Portland) Oregon. He actually built, with members of this new parish, the church and an apartment for his family. He subseq
2 CONC uently served parishes at Moose Lake (6yrs.), Barnesville (6yrs.), and Brainerd (24 yrs.), all in Minnesota. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his wife built a retirement home on Rice Lake near Brainerd, and lived there, enjoying gardening, entertaining his grandchildren with pontoon rides, traveling and visiting their children around the country until entering as
2 CONC sisted living in 2006. He and his wife lived in Northfield, MN for the past four years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife of 70 years, Phyllis; 6 children: M. Annette (Robert) Hanson of Boston, Massachusetts, Philip (Patricia Sausser) of St. Anthony, Krista (Giuseppe) Coco of Suffern, New York, Mark (Turi) of Moscow, Idaho,
2 CONC  Karina (Joel) Peterson of Brainerd, Elizabeth (John) Bade of Northfield; 10 grandchildren: Nels (Emily) Hanson, Per Hanson, Sonia Hoversten, Anne (Tom) Archambault, Alessandra Coco, Elizabeth Coco, Knut Hoversten, Liv Hoversten (
2 CONC Chris Sprague), Leif Bade and Bjorn Bade; 2 great-granddaughters: Katherine Hanson, Adelaide Archambault, and one on the way!; 4 brothers: Chris of Hendricks, Garfield of Edina, Vincent (Margery) of San Rafael, California, Kermit 
2 CONC (Ruth) of Austin; 2 sisters: Clara Amundson of Ivanhoe, Bernice Digre of Prior Lake; many nieces, nephews other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, his brothers Knut, Joseph, Emmanuel and his sisters Kristina Fixen, Ellen and Emma Hoversten and Esther Marie Christiansen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surrounded by the love of his wife and family, Chester passed away Monday morning, November 16, 2015, at Three Links Care Center in Northfield at the age of 93.
2 CONT
2 CONT A service to celebrate Chester's life will be held at 2:00 PM, Saturday, November 21, 2015,at St. John's Lutheran Church, 500 W. 3rd Street in Northfield. Visitation will be two hour prior to the service with a reception to follow
2 CONC . Interment will be in Hemnes Lutheran Cemetery, Minneota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials are preferred to Heifer Project and World Hunger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are with the Benson & Langehough Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *Phyllis Hoversten (1921 - 2016)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Hemnes Cemetery  Minneota Lyon County Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Jim Lee Record added: Nov 17, 2015  Find A Grave Memorial# 155115328
