1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martha, who was alert and active until the time of her death at almost 100 years, had a keen sense of humor and was always laughing and joking. She kept busy, even in her later years, knitting mittens and boots. Th
2 CONC e knit boots she wore around the house in place of shoes. She never lost interest in children. Those in our family even remember how she would feed Lester Larson (born May 1907) by first chewing the food well herself and then feed
2 CONC ing him. This was an old Norwegian custom among the people who got their bread from coarse grains. In America, Martha often stayed with her daughter and son-in-law Stine and John Larson. 
