1 NAME Ole /Olson/
2 GIVN Ole
2 SURN Olson
2 _MARNM Olson
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 FEB 1896
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 MAR 1957
2 PLAC buried Schie Lutheran Cemetery
2 ADDR
1 FAMS @F6000000083416083521@
1 RFN geni:6000000003887833206
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 NOTE
2 CONT March 21, 1957 - Ole Olson, son of the late Peter and Gertie Olson, was born on February 28, 1896 and departed from this world on March 8, 1957, having attained the age of 61 years and 8 days.
2 CONT On September 3, 1919, he was united in marriage to Manda Northouse. To this union were born three children:  Gorda (Mrs. Arnold Houskesr) of Spring Grove and Orvel and Perlind of Mabel, MN.  Survivors are his wife, three children,
2 CONC  grandchildren, Linda and Gary Housker; Sandra, Cheryl, Craig, Paul, Charles and Karen Olson; brothers, Martin and Albert of Harmony, Bennie and Thomas of Austin, Melvin of Mabel: sisters, Mrs. Ernest M. Erickson (Mary) of Spring 
2 CONC Grove and Mrs. Clarence Harkness (Ann) of Mabel; an uncle, Hans Saue of Colorado Springs, CO; an aunt, Mrs. P. E. Pederson of Montevideo, MN; nieces and nephews.  His parents and one sister (Mrs. Carl Opsahl, Ella) of Mendota, Ill
2 CONC  preceded him in death.  He moved with his parents to this vicinity in 1013 and since has been farming on various farms with the exception of time he spendt serving his country in World War I.  In 1838 he purchased the Jake Larson
2 CONC  farm and that since has been the family home.
2 CONT He was a member of the Scheie Lutheran Church and the American Legion.  He was loved by all children and especially dear to his heart were his own grandchildren.  Go and let my grave be made; Tired and weary now with straying, Far
2 CONC ewell to the earth I've said Heaven's call to peace obeying, Calls me now the halppy rest Of the angels ever blest.
1 SOUR
