2 ADDR
1 FAMC @F6000000083416083521@
1 RFN geni:6000000003888444785
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 NOTE
2 CONT He attended rural school.  He was a veteran of World War ll.  He farmed, then moved to Mabel in 1961.  He was a Fillmore County Deputy Sheriff for four years and Chief of Police in Mabel for 15 years.  He was a member of the Ameri
2 CONC can Legion Post 299 Mabel.  He was a member of the Mabel First Lutheran Church.  He is survived by six grandchildren; three step-grandchildren besides wife, children & brother & sister.  Funeral services were Thur at the Mabel Fir
2 CONC st Luthean church, the Rev Phillip Ruud officiated.  Burial was in the Mabel Lutheran Cemetery.
