2 TITL MHS Birth Certificate Index
1 NOTE
2 CONT Perlind Olson, 86, of Mabel
2 CONT Perlind J. Olson, 86, a lifelong Mabel area farmer, died Monday, Oct. 27, 2008, at the Gundersen-Lutheran Medical Center in La Crosse, Wis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born Jan. 10, 1922, in Preble Township, Fillmore County, to Ole and Manda (Northouse) Olson. He attended the Kelly School near the farm in Preble Township. On Nov. 24, 1944, he married Elvina S. Nerstad at the Scheie Luther
2 CONC an Church. She died Dec. 12, 1999.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olson lived and farmed his entire life in Preble Township. He was a member of the Scheie Lutheran Church, where he had served on the council; Farmer's Union; and NFO; and enjoyed being with family and friends, church activities, p
2 CONC laying cards, and horses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include two sons, Paul and Charles (Fay); and one daughter, Karen (Neil) Rasmussen, all of Mabel; five grandchildren, Heath and Adam Olson, Kimberlea Wagner, Tara Kreidermacher and Lance Rasmussen; five step grandchildre
2 CONC n Deanna, Sherry, Lisa, Todd, and Tony; nine great-grandchildren; eight step great-grandchildren; a sister, Gorda Housker of Mabel; and nieces and nephews. In addition to his wife, he was preceded in death by an infant son and a b
2 CONC rother, Orville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were Friday, Oct. 31, at the Scheie Lutheran Church in rural Mabel with the Rev. Mary Waudby officiating. Burial was in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mengis Funeral Home in Mabel assisted the family with arrangements.
