1 NOTE {geni:about_me}    Ulen - Raymond Trochmann, 93, Ulen, died Sunday, March 29, 2015, at Viking Manor Nursing Home in Ulen.
2 CONT     Funeral services will be held at 3 p.m. Tuesday, March 31, at Jevnaker Lutheran Church, rural Borup. Services will be led by Pastor Arlow Hushagen.  Special music will be provided by Lowell and Lona Trochmann and Laurie Baril.
2 CONC  Marla Hushagen will be the organist.  Serving as pallbearers will be Raymond’s grandsons Rick Tungseth, Rob Tungseth, Jamie Erickson, Micah Erickson, Mark Erickson and Jared Erickson. The honorary bearers will be his granddaughte
2 CONC rs, Lisa Trochmann, Sarah Eider, Laura Bennett and Lindsay Tungseth.
2 CONT     Visitation will be held Monday, March 30, from 5 to 7 p.m. with a prayer service at 6:30 p.m. at the Anderson Family Funeral Home, Twin Valley. Visitation will take place one hour prior to the service at the church on Tuesday.
2 CONC  Interment will be in Jevnaker Lutheran Cemetery, rural Borup.
2 CONT     Raymond Vernon Trochmann was born on the farm near Thief River Falls, on Oct. 26, 1921, to Anna (Wold) and Victor Trochmann. He attended country school through the eighth grade and graduated from Lincoln High School with the C
2 CONC lass of 1940.
2 CONT     Ray helped on the farm until he was called by the Lord to the ministry. In preparation for this ministry, he attended Augsburg College in Minneapolis. During his second year at Augsburg, Ray and a friend attended the Gateway G
2 CONC ospel Mission. It was here where Ray met the love of his life, Mildred Eastvold. They were united in marriage Nov. 27, 1948, at Jevnaker Lutheran Church, rural Borup.
2 CONT     The couple made their home in the Twin Cities area, where Ray worked for Johnson Electric Co. selling light fixtures. In 1956, an opportunity to purchase a farmstead near Mildred’s parents became available. They purchased the 
2 CONC farm east of Borup, where they raised their family and farmed for 40 years. Upon retirement, Ray and Mildred moved to Twin Valley for 14 years before moving to Northern Lights Assisted Living in Ulen. Ray recently moved into Vikin
2 CONC g Manor and Mildred remains in their apartment.  
2 CONT     Over the years, Ray was an active member of Jevnaker Lutheran Church and held the title of Sunday School superintendent for 15 years. He also held membership with the Ada-Mahnomen Gideons and was on both the Borup School Board
2 CONC  and Land-O-Lakes Board. In his spare time, Ray enjoyed carpentry and woodworking, and loved to listen, sing and make music.
2 CONT     Ray is survived by his wife of 66 years, Mildred, of Ulen; son, Raynard (Glenda) of Moorhead; daughters: Marilyn (Jim) Erickson of Fullerton, Calif., Rebekah (Charles) Woods of Sherwood, Ore., and Margaret (Dave) Tungseth of W
2 CONC hite Bear Lake; 10 grandchildren; 11 great-grandchildren; two step-grandchildren and several nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents; son Ronald in 1964; four brothers and four sisters. http://www.trftimes.com/
2 CONC obituaries/raymond-trochmann-93
