2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ==Esther Sundbom 1915-2003==
2 CONT Esther Sundbom, 88, of Bagley, died on Tuesday, September 16, 2003, at the Greensview Health Care Center in Bagley. She was born on August 8, 1915, at Trail, Minnesota, the daughter of Selmer and Selma (Jacobson) Wold. She was bap
2 CONC tized and confirmed at Zion Lutheran Church in rural Fosston. She attended rural country school by Trail and she worked out as a hired girl. Esther married Hugo Walter Sundbom on October 3, 1936 at Fosston. They bought a farm and 
2 CONC moved to Leonard in 1948. In the summer of 1959, they moved to Bagley. She was a homemaker her whole life. Hugo died on September 21, 1997. Esther was a member of Faith Lutheran Church in Bagley. She enjoyed scrap booking, rummage
2 CONC  sales, crocheting, embroidery, collecting recipes, cooking and coffee parties. She also loved to fish. She is survived by her two daughters, Dorothy (Wayne) Johnson, and Elaine (George) Larson, both of Bagley; three brothers, Llo
2 CONC yd (Carol) Wold of Trail, Kenneth (Arlene) Wold of Fosston; one sister, Myrtle Osmonson of Gully; 10 grandchildren; 19 great grandchildren and one great great grandchild. She was preceded in death by her husband, one granddaughter
2 CONC  and one grandson. Funeral services were held on Saturday, September, 20, at the Faith Lutheran Church in Bagley with the Reverends John Omans and Mardy Schermerhorn officiating. Interment was at the Bagley City Cemetery. The Ceas
2 CONC e Family Funeral Home of Bagley assisted the family with arrangements.
2 CONT
